  "data": {
    "ruleType": "army-rule",
    "summary": "With **LEAGUES OF VOTANN** as your [Army Faction](vsdata:core-rule/select-army-faction), your **LEAGUES OF VOTANN** units get either **Hostile Acquisition** or **Fortify Takeover**, never both, according to your Yield points (YP):\n\n- as the battle begins, they get Hostile Acquisition until [your next Command phase](vsdata:core-rule/command-phase)\n- as [your Command phase](vsdata:core-rule/command-phase) ends, they get Hostile Acquisition if you hold under 7YP, or Fortify Takeover if you hold 7YP or more, until your next Command phase\n\n**Hostile Acquisition**:\n\n- attacks by the unit's models against an enemy unit in range of an [objective marker](vsdata:core-rule/objectives) get +1 to [Hit](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls)\n- you can re-roll the unit's [Advance rolls](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move) and [Charge rolls](vsdata:core-rule/charge-step)\n\n**Fortify Takeover**:\n\n- while the unit is in range of an [objective marker](vsdata:core-rule/objectives) you control, attacks by its models against enemy units get +1 to [Hit](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls)\n- unless the unit is a **VEHICLE**, attacks against it whose S is greater than its T get -1 to [Wound](vsdata:core-rule/wound-rolls)\n\n**Yield Points**: as [either player's Command phase](vsdata:core-rule/command-phase) ends, controlling an objective marker in your deployment zone earns you 1YP. From battle round 2, you also gain 1YP for each of these that is true:\n\n- an objective marker outside your deployment zone is under your control\n- 2 or more objective markers outside your deployment zone are under your control\n- your opponent controls fewer objective markers than you\n\nIn your turn, these YP come in before you check which ability your units get. A rule that costs YP can be used only if you can pay all of it; paying lowers your YP, which never falls below 0.\n\n**Designer's Note**: rules that earn or spend YP let you steer which of the 2 abilities your units get. Your army switches ability only as your Command phase ends, so keeping or changing it can take planning.",
